    duplicate_of: []  # ff13
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ff13
    pr_ref:  # ff13
    description: "io-boundaries and verify-claims must report a call into an untraced installed dependency as \"untraced dependency, I/O unknown\", never as \"no I/O\". ADR-0016 keeps the shipped I/O catalogue stdlib-only and finds e.g. an LLM API call by tracing chain.run -> library internals -> httpx -> stdlib socket; when the dependency source is not analysed, that chain ends at a boundary stub and the network egress silently disappears. This is already true today for node_modules and venv site-packages (excluded by default), and becomes true for Mix deps/ once installed-dependency source is off by default -- so this must land before (or with) that change. Model it like unknown_dynamic (ADR-0016 §7). Community overlay rows for a third-party sink still count as detection."  # ff13
    fields: {}  # ff13
